## Add size and compare scaling

We compute \(Rg=\sqrt{Eigval1+Eigval2+Eigval3}\), which measures atomic
spread around the pocket center. We then use the same five measurements in
two PCAs, changing only scaling to identify its effect.

```{r pca-size}
# Add Rg and run the five-variable PCA before and after scaling.
d1$Rg <- sqrt(d1$Eigval.1 + d1$Eigval.2 + d1$Eigval.3)
five_input <- d1[c(five_names, "Origin")]

#without scale
pca3 <- PCA(five_input, scale.unit = FALSE, quali.sup = 6, graph = FALSE)
plot(pca3, choix = "var")
plot(pca3, choix = "ind", label="none", habillage = 6)
```

```{r}
#with scale
pca4 <- PCA(five_input, scale.unit = TRUE, quali.sup = 6, graph = FALSE)
plot(pca4, choix = "var")
plot(pca4, choix = "ind", label="none", habillage = 6)
```

